import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Signals, not noise."
	description="The Trend Times is an independent publication that tracks what people actually need, not what's loudest online."
	pubDate={new Date('2026-11-03')}
	updatedDate={new Date('2026-11-04')}
	eyebrow="ABOUT / OUR METHOD"
	showDate={false}
>
	<p>
		Every month, the internet produces an ocean of launches, hot takes, and viral demos. Very little
		of it tells you where real demand is forming. The Trend Times exists to close that gap: we read
		the noise so founders, builders, and investors can act on the signal.
	</p>

	<h2>The TTT standard</h2>
	<p>Every briefing follows the same three steps. Less hype, more evidence.</p>
	<ol>
		<li>
			<strong>Listen.</strong> We look for recurring pain across Reddit, X, Hacker News, and builder
			communities, over a rolling 30-day window.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Cross-check.</strong> We compare conversation velocity with repositories, pricing, and
			observable behavior. Attention is not intent, and intent is not spending.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Distill.</strong> We publish the useful takeaway, our confidence level, and what remains
			unproven.
		</li>
	</ol>

	<h2>Editorial standards</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Every number in a briefing links to the post, repository, or market it came from.</li>
		<li>We state our confidence level and what we could not verify.</li>
		<li>We do not accept payment for coverage. Advertising, if shown, is served by third parties and never shapes what we write.</li>
		<li>When we get something wrong, we fix it and note the change and date at the end of the article.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>What we are not</h2>
	<p>
		We are not a news wire, and we do not give investment advice. Read our <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> for
		the full terms.
	</p>

